upstairs upstairs  scenes of panic on the outskirts of the  danish capital  people ran for their lives as shots were  fired in the fields shopping mall  witnesses said people hid in shops  terrified as a man walked round with a  hunting rifle  it's pure terror this is awful you know  you might wonder how a person can do  this to other human beings but it's  beyond beyond  you know anything that's possible we  didn't know what to do so we ran  people were guiding us towards the exit  sign and then  we ran up the roof and were stuck there  for a while and then people were  panicking all over the place and people  crying  armed officers were quickly on the scene  as were paramedics and firefighters  police arrested a suspect in the  immediate aftermath of the attack  describing him as a 22 year old ethnic  dane and saying that several people had  been killed at around 1am local time the  streets around field shopping center  were still blocked off as police held a  press conference to update the number of  dead and wounded  police say the motive was unclear and  would not rule out what they called an  act of terrorism  we have a situation where we have three  dead it's a man in his forties and two  young people  the shopping centers just across from a  subway line connecting the city centre  with the international airport  tourists arriving into the country were  held away from their hotels near fields  until late into the night  while a concert by pop star harry styles  was at first given the go-ahead after  organisers spoke with police before  eventually being cancelled  the suspect in sunday's shooting will  now face a judge for questioning on  monday  paul reese aljazeera copenhagen
 

